# Eligibility engine
Port data/reference_engine.py; results must equal data/expected.json exactly.

Criterion -> TRUE | FALSE | UNKNOWN | N/A
- 'when' false -> N/A; 'when' unknown -> UNKNOWN; field missing -> UNKNOWN;
  value in unknown_values -> UNKNOWN; else apply op (eq, neq, in, not_in, gt, gte, lt, lte,
  between, is_true, is_false).

Scheme status, in this order:
1. status == "announced" -> WATCHLIST
2. kind == "registration" and already registered -> NOT_APPLICABLE
3. hard FALSE exists: all have "fix" and count <= 2 -> NEAR_MISS, else NOT_ELIGIBLE
4. hard UNKNOWN exists -> LIKELY
5. else ELIGIBLE
Counts: met = hard TRUE, total = hard non-N/A, unknown = hard UNKNOWN.

Derived fields (derive.py): enterprise_size (1 Apr 2025 limits: micro <= 2.5 cr investment AND
<= 10 cr turnover; small 25/100; medium 125/500), pmegp_special, female_or_scst,
similar_loan_last_5y, udyogini_income_ok. See AGENTS.md 2.3.

Estimators return {grant_min, grant_max, credit}. Path planner: candidates = ELIGIBLE/LIKELY/
NEAR_MISS, not registration, grant_max > 0; drop subsets containing a conflict pair; keep maximal
subsets; sort by grant_max desc. Never add credit to grants.
Display: Udyam Assist only if no PAN; WATCHLIST only if no hard FALSE; hide NOT_APPLICABLE.
Every function gets a pytest test.
